---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is the minimum contract duration?",
    a: "We ask for an initial three-month commitment, because SEO needs that long to take measurable effect. After that, the agreement rolls monthly and you may cancel with 30 days' notice. Clients who continue do so because they observe results, not because a long contract obliges them to."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you guarantee first-page rankings?",
    a: "No reputable SEO provider can guarantee specific rankings, as Google's algorithm considers in excess of 200 factors. What we guarantee is transparent reporting, ethical practices, and a clear strategy tied to measurable KPIs such as organic traffic, leads, and revenue."
  },
  {
    q: "What is encompassed within the monthly retainer?",
    a: "Every retainer includes technical SEO monitoring, content creation, on-page optimisation, local SEO management, and regular reporting. The precise scope is determined by your tier. We additionally provide ad-hoc support for questions and prompt fixes."
  },
  {
    q: "When should results be expected?",
    a: "Most Reading businesses observe measurable improvements within 3-4 months. Local SEO gains (Google Maps, the local pack) often materialise more rapidly, within 4-8 weeks. Competitive terms such as \"solicitors reading\" or \"accountants reading\" typically require 4-6 months to shift significantly."
  },
  {
    q: "Why are your fees lower than those of London agencies?",
    a: "Lower overheads. We do not maintain a Shoreditch office lease, nor do we interpose an account manager layer between you and the strategist. You work directly with a senior SEO consultant who operates in Reading. The expertise is equivalent; the postcode premium is removed."
  },
  {
    q: "Is it possible to switch tiers or cancel?",
    a: "Yes. You may upgrade, downgrade, or cancel with 30 days' notice. Should your business grow and require additional content or link building, we scale accordingly. If budgets contract, we scale down to safeguard the gains already secured."
  }
];

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://seoreading.uk/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services", "item": "https://seoreading.uk/services/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "SEO Pricing Reading", "item": "https://seoreading.uk/seo-pricing-reading/" }
  ]
};

const webPageSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "SEO Pricing Reading | Transparent Costs",
  "description": "Transparent SEO pricing for Reading businesses. Monthly retainers from £500, one-off audits from £300. Typically 40-60% less than London agencies.",
  "url": "https://seoreading.uk/seo-pricing-reading/",
  "isPartOf": { "@type": "WebSite", "name": "SEO Reading", "url": "https://seoreading.uk/" },
  "breadcrumb": { "@id": "https://seoreading.uk/seo-pricing-reading/#breadcrumb" }
};

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": f.q,
    "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a }
  }))
};

const serviceSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "SEO Services Reading",
  "provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "SEO Reading", "sameAs": [] },
  "areaServed": { "@type": "City", "name": "Reading" },
  "hasOfferCatalog": {
    "@type": "OfferCatalog",
    "name": "SEO Packages",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "Offer",
        "name": "Starter SEO Package",
        "priceSpecification": { "@type": "PriceSpecification", "price": "500", "priceCurrency": "GBP", "unitText": "MONTH" }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Offer",
        "name": "Growth SEO Package",
        "priceSpecification": { "@type": "PriceSpecification", "price": "1000", "priceCurrency": "GBP", "unitText": "MONTH" }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Offer",
        "name": "Enterprise SEO Package",
        "priceSpecification": { "@type": "PriceSpecification", "price": "2000", "priceCurrency": "GBP", "unitText": "MONTH" }
      }
    ]
  }
};

const schema = [breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema, faqSchema, serviceSchema];
---

<Base
  title="SEO Pricing Reading | Transparent Costs"
  description="Transparent SEO pricing for Reading businesses. Monthly retainers from £500, one-off audits from £300. Typically 40-60% less than London agencies."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 dot-grid-light pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="absolute -bottom-20 -left-32 w-[300px] h-[300px] rounded-full opacity-10 blur-[80px] aurora-1" style="background: radial-gradient(circle, #D4AF37, transparent 70%);" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto relative z-10">
      <h1 class="fade-up">SEO Pricing for Reading Businesses</h1>
      <p class="subtitle fade-up" style="transition-delay: 80ms;">Transparent SEO pricing for Reading businesses. Tiered packages from one-off audits to monthly retainers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="prose fade-up">

      <p>SEO Reading provides transparent, competitive pricing for businesses in Reading and Berkshire, typically 40-60% less than equivalent London agencies, whilst delivering the same calibre of expertise with deeper local knowledge.</p>

      <p>Every business presents different objectives, competitive landscapes, and starting positions. A cafe on <strong>Broad Street</strong> competing for "brunch reading" requires a different investment than a law firm at <strong>Forbury Square</strong> targeting "commercial solicitors berkshire." The pricing below reflects that reality accordingly.</p>

      <div class="quick-answer">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> SEO pricing in Reading ranges from £300 for a one-off audit to £500-£2,000/month for ongoing retainers. Most Reading SMEs invest £750-£1,200/month for meaningful organic growth.
      </div>

      <p>We publish our prices because concealed pricing wastes everyone's time. Below you will find our three monthly retainer tiers, one-off service costs, and a direct comparison against typical London agency fees.</p>

      <h2>Pricing Tiers</h2>

    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 my-8">

      <div class="pricing-tier">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Starter</p>
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand mb-1">£500<span class="text-base font-normal text-text-muted">/month</span></p>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mb-4">For small Reading businesses</p>
        <ul class="text-sm space-y-2 mb-6">
          <li>Monthly technical SEO monitoring</li>
          <li>2 optimised content pieces per month</li>
          <li>Local SEO management (Google Business Profile)</li>
          <li>Monthly performance report</li>
          <li>On-page optimisation for key pages</li>
          <li>Core Web Vitals monitoring</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-muted"><strong>Best for:</strong> Cafes near Broad Street, independent shops, local tradespeople, new businesses establishing their first organic presence.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pricing-tier featured">
        <span class="absolute -top-3 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 bg-accent text-brand-dark text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full">Most Popular</span>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Growth</p>
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand mb-1">£1,000<span class="text-base font-normal text-text-muted">/month</span></p>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mb-4">For established Reading businesses</p>
        <ul class="text-sm space-y-2 mb-6">
          <li>Full technical SEO audit and ongoing fixes</li>
          <li>4 optimised content pieces per month</li>
          <li>Link building (outreach and digital PR)</li>
          <li>Local SEO management</li>
          <li>Competitor tracking and gap analysis</li>
          <li>Fortnightly reporting with strategy calls</li>
          <li>Schema markup implementation</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-muted"><strong>Best for:</strong> Estate agents, accountancy firms, law firms at Forbury Square, dental practices, and established service businesses positioned for growth.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pricing-tier">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Enterprise</p>
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand mb-1">£2,000<span class="text-base font-normal text-text-muted">/month</span></p>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mb-4">For larger organisations and multi-location</p>
        <ul class="text-sm space-y-2 mb-6">
          <li>Everything in Growth, plus:</li>
          <li>AI search optimisation (ChatGPT, Copilot, Perplexity)</li>
          <li>Advanced schema and entity strategy</li>
          <li>Weekly reporting with priority Slack/email support</li>
          <li>Dedicated SEO strategist</li>
          <li>Multi-location or multi-service campaign management</li>
          <li>Conversion rate optimisation recommendations</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs text-text-muted"><strong>Best for:</strong> Companies at Green Park, Thames Valley Park, multi-branch businesses, and organisations targeting national terms alongside local.</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="prose">

      <p>All tiers include direct access to a senior SEO consultant, no junior account managers, no intermediaries. You communicate with the individual conducting the work.</p>

      <h2>One-Off Services</h2>

      <p>Not every business requires a monthly retainer. Should you need a specific piece of work completed, these one-off services address the most common requests we receive from Reading businesses.</p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Service</th>
            <th>Starting Price</th>
            <th>What You Receive</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/seo-audit-reading/">SEO Audit</a></td>
            <td>£300</td>
            <td>Full technical, on-page, and competitive audit with prioritised action plan</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/technical-seo-reading/">Technical SEO Fix</a></td>
            <td>£500</td>
            <td>Hands-on implementation: crawl errors, Core Web Vitals, indexation issues, site speed</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Content Strategy</td>
            <td>£400</td>
            <td>Keyword research, topical mapping, content calendar, competitor gap analysis</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/ai-search-optimisation-reading/">AI Search Optimisation Setup</a></td>
            <td>£750</td>
            <td>Entity optimisation, structured data, llms.txt, citation-ready content restructuring</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>One-off services are typically delivered within 5-10 working days. Payment terms are 50% upfront and 50% upon delivery.</p>

      <h2>Reading vs London: Price Comparison</h2>

      <p>Reading businesses are frequently approached by London agencies first. The resulting sticker shock is considerable. Below is a direct comparison of what equivalent services cost.</p>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Service</th>
            <th>London Agency (Typical)</th>
            <th>SEO Reading</th>
            <th>Saving</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Monthly SEO retainer</td>
            <td>£2,000-£5,000</td>
            <td>£500-£2,000</td>
            <td>40-75%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>SEO audit</td>
            <td>£1,000-£3,000</td>
            <td>£300-£600</td>
            <td>60-80%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Content (per piece)</td>
            <td>£300-£600</td>
            <td>£150-£300</td>
            <td>50%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Technical SEO fix</td>
            <td>£1,500-£3,000</td>
            <td>£500-£1,000</td>
            <td>60-70%</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Link building (per month)</td>
            <td>£1,000-£2,500</td>
            <td>£400-£1,000</td>
            <td>50-60%</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>The quality gap that many assume exists between London and Reading SEO consultancies is, in our experience, a misconception. The tools are identical (Ahrefs, Screaming Frog, Search Console). The knowledge is equivalent. The distinction is that a Reading-based consultancy understands Reading's market, knows which local directories carry weight, and does not pass on the cost of a Farringdon office lease.</p>

      <p>A Reading-based consultancy also comprehends the local commercial landscape: the Thames Valley technology corridor, the concentration of professional services within the town centre, and the commuter-belt dynamics that make local search intent materially different from central London.</p>

      <h2>What Affects SEO Pricing</h2>

      <p>No two SEO campaigns carry the same cost. Four factors drive price variation for Reading businesses:</p>

      <h3>1. Competition Level</h3>

      <p>A plumber in Tilehurst faces less online competition than a personal injury solicitor in Reading town centre. Greater competition necessitates more content, more link building, and more time to achieve rankings. Competitive verticals such as law, finance, and property in Reading typically require the Growth or Enterprise tier.</p>

      <h3>2. Current Site State</h3>

      <p>A newly launched website with no domain authority requires foundational work before it can compete. An established site with existing rankings may only need technical fixes and content gaps addressed. We assess this during the <a href="/seo-audit-reading/">initial audit</a> and recommend a tier based upon what your site genuinely requires, not what generates the greatest fee for us.</p>

      <h3>3. Goals and Timeline</h3>

      <p>Targeting "reading restaurants" for a new bistro is achievable within 3-4 months at Starter level. Targeting "best estate agents reading" against established firms with years of domain authority requires Growth level and 6+ months. We set realistic expectations from the outset, grounded in data rather than vague assurances.</p>

      <h3>4. Industry Regulations</h3>

      <p>YMYL (Your Money or Your Life) sectors (health, finance, legal) face more stringent quality thresholds in Google. A financial adviser in Reading requires E-E-A-T signals (credentials, authoritative content, trust markers) that a florist does not. This additional content and authority-building work is reflected in the pricing accordingly.</p>

      <h2>ROI of SEO for Reading Businesses</h2>

      <p>SEO is an investment, and you can model your own numbers with our free <a href="/tools/seo-roi-calculator/">SEO ROI calculator</a>. The following worked example illustrates how to consider the return. The figures are illustrative estimates drawn from typical keyword-tool averages and industry click-through data, not a projection or guarantee for any specific business.</p>

      <p><strong>Example: a Reading estate agent.</strong> The keyword "estate agents reading" generates approximately 1,300 searches per month. Position 1 captures roughly 28% of clicks; that equates to 364 visitors per month. The Google Ads equivalent cost for those clicks is approximately £2.50 per click, yielding a traffic value of <strong>£910 per month</strong> from a single keyword.</p>

      <p>At our Growth tier (£1,000/month), that one keyword alone would nearly cover the entire investment. In practice, a well-executed SEO campaign targets dozens of related terms: "estate agents in reading berkshire," "best letting agents reading," "property valuations RG1." The compounding effect means a well-executed campaign can exceed a 3:1 return within 6-12 months, although outcomes depend on competition and starting position.</p>

      <p>Unlike PPC, SEO traffic does not cease when you stop investing. Rankings established over 12 months continue to generate traffic even if you pause your campaign. That residual value is what renders SEO the highest-ROI marketing channel for most Reading businesses.</p>

      <p>Local service businesses realise particularly strong returns because local search intent converts at substantially higher rates than generic informational searches. An individual searching "emergency plumber reading" is prepared to purchase immediately.</p>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      {faqs.map(f => (
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">{f.q}</h3>
          <p>{f.a}</p>
        </div>
      ))}

      <div class="cta-box">
        <h2>Request Your Free SEO Audit</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-200 mt-2">Discover precisely where your Reading business stands in search. No obligation, no jargon, simply a clear report detailing what is working, what is not, and what to address first.</p>
        <a href="/free-seo-audit-reading/">Book a Consultation</a>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-text-muted">Prepared to discuss your SEO requirements? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a> or explore our full range of <a href="/services/">SEO services</a> for Reading businesses.</p>

    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
